# 64. Security Investigation Exercise

Create:

```bash
mkdir security_lab
cd security_lab

touch normal.txt
touch sensitive.txt
touch executable.sh
```

Set:

```bash
chmod 644 normal.txt
chmod 600 sensitive.txt
chmod 755 executable.sh
```

Now investigate:

```bash
ls -la
```

Then:

```bash
stat normal.txt
stat sensitive.txt
stat executable.sh
```

Ask yourself:

```text
Who owns each file?

What group owns each file?

Who can read it?

Who can modify it?

Who can execute it?

Which file is most protected?

Which file is executable?

```

